  Slug: alchemical-sciences-methodology
  DisplayName: Alchemical Sciences Methodology
  IconPath: icons/sundries/books/book-embossed-jewel-blue-red.webp
  Description: Your methodology emphasizes chemical and alchemical analysis, collecting
    information from unusual particles and fluids found on the scene. You possess
    enough alchemical know-how to whip up a few tinctures to help you with your cases.
    You're trained in Crafting and gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Alchemical
    Crafting] skill feat. You start with a standard formula book, which contains
    the formulas for two common 1st-level alchemical items of your choice (these
    must be elixirs or tools), in addition to the formulas gained from Alchemical
    Crafting. Each time you gain a level, you learn the formula for one common alchemical
    elixir or alchemical tool of any level of item you can create. During your daily
    preparations, you can create a number of versatile vials equal to your Intelligence
    modifier. Statistics for versatile vials appear in the alchemist class. You gain
    the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Quick Tincture] action, which you
    can use to turn one of these vials into an elixir or alchemical tool for which
    you know the formula. If you have the ability to create versatile vials from
    more than one source (such as the alchemist multiclass archetype), you can use
    any of your versatile vials for any ability you have that requires them.
